# Generated by Cargo
target/

# Signing material never enters this repository. The repo is public.
*.jks
*.p12
*.p8
*.mobileprovision

# Generated by `tauri android init` / `tauri ios init`.
#
# Almost all of gen/ is regenerated on every CI run and must stay ignored, but
# Tauri gives Android no template hook — there is no `bundle.android.template`
# to match the iOS one (checked against the config schema), so an Android build
# decision has nowhere to live except the generated Gradle file itself. So a
# THREE-file allowlist is tracked, and everything else in gen/ is ignored.
#
# This is safe because `tauri android init` does NOT overwrite a file that
# already exists (verified by experiment): CI re-inits to regenerate buildSrc,
# the res/ tree and the launcher mipmaps, and the three files below survive.
#
# That same "never overwrites" property is what makes these files go STALE
# silently on a @tauri-apps/cli bump. The `dynawalla-android-gen` job in
# ci.yml is the gate for it: it regenerates the template into a scratch tree
# and diffs it against ../android-template-baseline/.
#
# The iOS side needs no allowlist: `bundle.iOS.template` points the CLI at the
# committed src-tauri/ios/project.yml, so gen/apple can stay fully generated.
# MainActivity.kt is in the allowlist for a different reason than the other
# two: once ANY part of gen/android is committed, `tauri android init` finds
# the directory on a fresh checkout and hard-errors unless the Java package
# directory exists too — with a message blaming the bundle identifier. See the
# comment at the top of that file.
/gen/**
!/gen/android/
!/gen/android/app/
!/gen/android/app/build.gradle.kts
!/gen/android/app/src/
!/gen/android/app/src/main/
!/gen/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
!/gen/android/app/src/main/java/
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, and
# `/gen/**` excludes the inc/corpora/dynawalla package directories too. This
# line re-includes the directories only; files under them stay ignored unless
# named below.
!/gen/android/app/src/main/java/**/
!/gen/android/app/src/main/java/**/MainActivity.kt

# The repository root .gitignore ignores Cargo.lock everywhere, from a stale
# workspace-era TODO. This manifest is its own workspace root and its lock file
# is part of the shipped build (ADR-0011 point 2): a store binary has to be
# reproducible from the tag. Corpán's lock is tracked for the same reason.
!Cargo.lock
